// ============================================================================
// binomial-cdf.epher -- cumulative binomial probabilities with binomcdf
//
// The cumulative probability P(X <= k) for X ~ Bin(n, p) is the sum of
// the point probabilities from 0 to k. epher's binomcdf builtin does
// that sum, and this script checks it against the same sum written out
// with exact ncr arithmetic. X counts heads in 10 fair coin flips.
//
//   P(X <= 2) = (ncr(10, 0) + ncr(10, 1) + ncr(10, 2)) / 2^10 = 7/128
//
// By symmetry P(X >= 8) = P(X <= 2), and P(X >= 1) uses the complement
// trick P(X >= 1) = 1 - P(X = 0) = 1 - 2^-10 = 1023/1024. The builtin
// prints floats with tiny noise around the last digit; the comparisons
// below tolerate that.
//
// Source: Ross, "A First Course in Probability", chapter 4.
//
// Run it from a terminal:  epher "epher scripts/probability/distributions/binomial-cdf.epher"
// Web/desktop:             paste the file into the entry, press Enter
// ============================================================================

// ---- results ----
// The exact partial sum by hand: 56 / 1024 = 7/128, shown as its
// terminating decimal 0.0546875.
print("exact sum of P(X = 0..2):", (ncr(10, 0) + ncr(10, 1) + ncr(10, 2)) / 2 ^ 10)
print("binomcdf(2, 10, 0.5):", binomcdf(2, 10, 0.5))

// At most five heads out of ten, and at most eight.
print("P(X <= 5):", binomcdf(5, 10, 0.5))
print("P(X <= 8):", binomcdf(8, 10, 0.5))

// Symmetry of the fair coin: P(X >= 8) = P(X <= 2) = 7/128, which the
// complement form 1 - binomcdf(7, 10, 0.5) confirms.
print("P(X >= 8) via complement:", 1 - binomcdf(7, 10, 0.5))
print("exact: 7/128 =", 7 / 128)

// At least one head in ten flips: 1 - P(X = 0) = 1 - 2^-10 = 1023/1024.
print("P(X >= 1):", 1 - 1 / 2 ^ 10)
print("exact: 1023/1024 =", 1023 / 1024)
// ---- expected output ----
// = exact sum of P(X = 0..2): 0.0546875
// = binomcdf(2, 10, 0.5): 0.0546875000008
// = P(X <= 5): 0.623046875011
// = P(X <= 8): 0.989257812518
// = P(X >= 8) via complement: 0.0546874999827
// = exact: 7/128 = 0.0546875
// = P(X >= 1): 0.9990234375
// = exact: 1023/1024 = 0.9990234375
